Troubleshooting Common Issues
Issue 1: Service Account Token Not Found
Problem: Error message "secrets not found" when extracting tokens.

Solution:

# For Kubernetes 1.24+, create tokens manually
kubectl create token alpha-user -n tenant-alpha --duration=24h
Issue 2: Permission Denied Errors
Problem: Tenants cannot access their own resources.

Solution:

# Check role bindings
kubectl get rolebindings -n tenant-alpha -o yaml

# Verify service account exists
kubectl get serviceaccounts -n tenant-alpha
Issue 3: Network Policy Blocking Legitimate Traffic
Problem: Pods cannot communicate with allowed services.

Solution:

# Check network policy configuration
kubectl describe networkpolicy tenant-alpha-isolation -n tenant-alpha

# Verify namespace labels
kubectl get namespaces --show-labels
Issue 4: Cross-Cluster Access Issues
Problem: Cannot access resources in the second cluster.

Solution:

# Verify cluster contexts
kubectl config get-contexts

# Check if RBAC is applied to both clusters
kubectl config use-context cluster-b
